---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { tree } from "../data/tree";
const title = "Practical AI workflows";
const description = "Build better AI workflows with worked guides, original experiments, open tools and reusable context. Start with a small task you can check.";
const blog = await getCollection("blog");
const skills = await getCollection("skills");
const conceptRoots = ["ai-llm-engineering", "software-engineering", "writing-and-documentation"]
  .map((slug) => tree.nodes[slug]).filter(Boolean);
const featured = [
  { id: "state-that-survives-the-session", kind: "Architecture guide", outcome: "Resume work without replaying everything", note: "Separate a small handoff from a durable recall store. Includes design choices and the measurements still needed." },
  { id: "keyword-plus-vector", kind: "Implementation report", outcome: "Find the exact flag your agent missed", note: "See how keyword and hybrid retrieval handle literal tokens, with queries, failure cases and commands." },
  { id: "anchors-that-point-nowhere", kind: "Repair report", outcome: "Check whether your citations actually resolve", note: "Follow a broken-anchor investigation from the extraction bug to a reproducible validation step." },
].map((pick) => ({ ...pick, entry: blog.find((post) => post.id === pick.id) })).filter((pick) => pick.entry);
---
<Base title={title} heading="Build better AI workflows." description={description} route="/" twin={null}>
  <p class="eyebrow">Guides, experiments & open tools</p>
  <p class="lede">Keep useful context. Find the evidence. Pick the tool that helps with the work in front of you.</p>
  <p class="hero-support">LLMSX is for developers and technical users working with AI agents. Start with a worked example, inspect the result, then reuse the instructions or reference files in your own setup.</p>
  <p class="hero-actions">
    <a class="btn" href="/start-here/" data-track="home_cta_click" data-cta-id="start-here">Try your first workflow</a>
    <a class="btn secondary" href="/blog/" data-track="home_cta_click" data-cta-id="read-research">Read the guides & research</a>
  </p>
  <p class="home-access">Read the guides and download reference files without an account.</p>

  <section class="home-feature" aria-labelledby="feature-title">
    <div>
      <p class="content-kind">Original experiment · 256 agent runs</p>
      <h2 id="feature-title">Do better docs actually save an AI agent money?</h2>
      <p>On two small repositories, llms files and search indexes on disk did not produce measurable savings. Loading documentation into the agent’s context did. That distinction changes what is worth building.</p>
      <p>The write-up includes the questions, raw results, correctness checks, failed setups and limits of the experiment.</p>
      <a href="/blog/what-docs-llms-files-and-indexes-actually-save/" data-track="card_click" data-card="original-experiment">Read the experiment →</a>
    </div>
    <aside class="feature-evidence" aria-label="Experiment scope">
      <strong>What you can inspect</strong>
      <dl>
        <dt>Scope</dt><dd>Two repositories, one model</dd>
        <dt>Comparison</dt><dd>Eight setups, repeated questions</dd>
        <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Public harness and raw results</dd>
        <dt>Limit</dt><dd>These results do not establish universal savings</dd>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="guides-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="guides-title">Solve a concrete problem</h2><a href="/blog/">All guides & research →</a></div>
    <ul class="home-guide-grid">
      {featured.map((pick) => (
        <li><p class="content-kind">{pick.kind}</p><h3><a href={`/blog/${pick.id}/`} data-track="card_click" data-card={pick.id}>{pick.outcome}</a></h3><p>{pick.note}</p></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="tools-title">Choose a tool for your task</h2><a href="/downloads/">Requirements & installation →</a></div>
    <p class="section-intro">Three separate terminal workbenches. Choose the one that matches the job; you do not need the whole stack.</p>
    <ul class="home-tool-list">
      <li><div><h3><a href="/explorer/">LLMSX Explorer</a></h3><p>Browse the concept library, keep notes and organize research jobs in a terminal workbench.</p></div><a class="tool-action" href="/downloads/#llmsx">Get LLMSX →</a></li>
      <li id="skills-explorer"><div><h3><a href="/downloads/#skills-explorer">Skills Explorer</a></h3><p>Inspect, edit and maintain the skills already installed across your agent harnesses.</p></div><a class="tool-action" href="/downloads/#skills-explorer-install">Get Skills Explorer →</a></li>
      <li id="github-explorer"><div><h3><a href="/downloads/#github-explorer">GitHub Explorer</a></h3><p>Browse a repository, edit with Vim and inspect Git and GitHub commands before running them.</p></div><a class="tool-action" href="/downloads/#github-explorer-setup">Get GitHub Explorer →</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="home-access">Want instructions instead of an app? <a href="/skills/">Browse {skills.length} reusable agent skills</a> and read each full prompt before installing it.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section home-library" aria-labelledby="library-title">
    <div>
      <p class="content-kind">Connected reference library</p><h2 id="library-title">Explore the concept tree.</h2>
      <p>Browse a topic, inspect its published reference and follow its sources. Download the facts as Markdown when you want to use them with an agent.</p>
      <p>The library includes agent-assisted research and mirrored source reports. Source links help you check a claim; they do not certify it.</p>
      <ul class="concept-preview" aria-label="A preview of the concept tree">
        {conceptRoots.map((root) => (
          <li><a href={`/tree/${root.slug}/`}>{root.concept}</a>
            <ul>{root.children.filter((child) => tree.nodes[child.slug]).slice(0, 3).map((child) => (
              <li><a href={`/tree/${child.slug}/`}>{child.concept}</a></li>
            ))}</ul>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/tree/" data-track="home_cta_click" data-cta-id="browse-concept-tree">Open the full interactive tree →</a> · <a href="/tree/3d/">Explore in 3D</a></p>
    </div>
    <ul class="resource-links">
      <li><a href="/context/">Download context files</a><span>Research reports and facts, sized for loading · <a href="/context.md">Markdown index</a></span></li>
      <li><a href="/directory/">Inspect the source directory</a><span>llms files scored for format quality</span></li>
      <li><a href="/reference/">Read the technical reference</a><span>Formats, lint rules and publishing conventions</span></li>
      <li><a href="/examples/">Use the code examples</a><span>Copyable recipes with stated assumptions</span></li>
      <li><a href="/demo/">Inspect the retrieval demo</a><span>A recorded keyword, vector and hybrid comparison</span></li>
      <li><a href="/family/">Load the site through llms.txt</a><span>An index for agents, with links to the published files</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <p class="home-editorial">An open project by <a href="/about/">Mitch Hudson</a>. Read <a href="/editorial/">how to interpret the sources and results</a>, or <a href="https://github.com/mithudso/llms-explorer/issues">report a correction</a>.</p>
</Base>
